[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/9219011","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/2489#issuecomment-9219011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/2489","id":9219011,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkyMTkwMTE=","user":{"login":"apendua","id":1971195,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NzExOTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1971195?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua","html_url":"https://github.com/apendua","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-10-08T08:17:54Z","updated_at":"2012-10-08T08:17:54Z","body":"@oal Basically, the code responsible for this behavior can be found [here](https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/master/src/extras/renderers/plugins/ShadowMapPlugin.js#L265-281):\n\n```\nif ( object.customDepthMaterial ) {\n\n    material = object.customDepthMaterial;\n\n} else if ( object instanceof THREE.SkinnedMesh ) {\n\n    material = object.geometry.morphTargets.length ? _depthMaterialMorphSkin : _depthMaterialSkin;\n\n} else if ( object.geometry.morphTargets.length ) {\n\n   material = _depthMaterialMorph;\n\n} else {\n\n    material = _depthMaterial;\n\n}\n```\n\nSo as you can see, the decision about shader parameters is being made based on your model attributes rather than on the current object's `material`. Maybe @mrdoob, or @alteredq could explain to you why it works this way :)\n\nHowever, If you want to change this behavior you can provide `object.customDepthMaterial` (as you can see in the code above). Before creating one, just look at these [examples](https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/master/src/extras/renderers/plugins/ShadowMapPlugin.js#L25-28):\n\n```\n_depthMaterial = new THREE.ShaderMaterial( { fragmentShader: depthShader.fragmentShader, vertexShader: depthShader.vertexShader, uniforms: depthUniforms } );\n_depthMaterialMorph = new THREE.ShaderMaterial( { fragmentShader: depthShader.fragmentShader, vertexShader: depthShader.vertexShader, uniforms: depthUniforms, morphTargets: true } );\n_depthMaterialSkin = new THREE.ShaderMaterial( { fragmentShader: depthShader.fragmentShader, vertexShader: depthShader.vertexShader, uniforms: depthUniforms, skinning: true } );\n_depthMaterialMorphSkin = new THREE.ShaderMaterial( { fragmentShader: depthShader.fragmentShader, vertexShader: depthShader.vertexShader, uniforms: depthUniforms, morphTargets: true, skinning: true } );\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/9219011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"apendua","id":1971195,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NzExOTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1971195?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua","html_url":"https://github.com/apendua","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apendua/subscrip